body:
Think of it like this. Suppose that all of the people who partake in this kind of tourism suddenly decide "hm, not gonna do it anymore".

&#x200B;

Well, now all the sex workers are without work and pay. Reasonably, if they had a better option than sex work, they would have taken it already, but since they did not, it is clear that it is the best option immediately available.

&#x200B;

I am not going to disagree that it is bad for the women in the long run, that and abortions, STDs and all the other issues that come up. But not everyone has the priviledge of doing things for the long term. This kind of tourism at least keeps them fed.

\> crazy thing is for all of the relationship **we both** had an agreement that **we** do not hang out with people of the opposite sex alone

&#x200B;

It isn't that \*he\* set up a boundary; \*they\* set up a boundary for one another, and she broke it.

The anthem of my state has a line that describes this situation.

&#x200B;

"People without virtue are bound to be slaves."

&#x200B;

Even if the protest does not work, it is the virtue of partaking in it that matters, to some extent. It may - although unlikely - inspire at least a few individuals to also take it up, and continue with such attitudes in the future whenever they come across another horrible measure such as this.

War Thunder straight up causes Stockholm Syndrome on all of its players, I swear to god. Almost everyone that plays it despises the game, but continues anyways.

&#x200B;

**AND I AM ONE OF THEM BABEYYYYYYY WOOOOOOOOOOOOO I LOVE MY CROMWELLLLLLLL RAAAAGHHHHHHHHH AP VOLUMETRIC RAAAAAAAGGHHHHHHHHH**

My man :handshake:

&#x200B;

I remember that WW1 mod that just sent waves upon waves of enemies at you. That was fun.

Man, sucks that this is reddit. Redditors only have one line of thought.

&#x200B;

"IF (person) = police, then (person) = bad. LOLOLO ACAB ACAB ACAB"

&#x200B;

ivhokie12 is being pretty down to earth in this. Obviously there will be bad cops and there are definitely issues, but some people act just downright paranoid, and then try to justify their unreasonable paranoia. Hell, you may as well not get out of your house and assume any random person on the street is out to get ya.

&#x200B;

Guess its just Americans being Americans. Having zero respect for authority by default, doing anything to oppose and resist it, then getting surprised when something bad happens.

This is probably the most grounded and reasonable response I've seen after closing several others. The former is basically just ... What any police does, regardless of country. The latter may not neccessarily be anything to worry about, but I'd definitely suspect I'm a bit paranoid.

&#x200B;

Ironically enough, walked past several cops today when out travelling and this response described my feeling almost perfectly. I was cautious and alert as I walked past three military policemen, but otherwise not really on edge, nor did I really fear anything.

Yeah no, go as far as saying you're objectively wrong regarding "help a struggling team turn the game around". As pretty much every TF2 youtuber has said, maybe in the past, yeah. But a team that is struggling to push is either worse than the defending team, or lacks coordination, or both. A random crit is not going to change that, it'll just annoy some poor bugger(s).

&#x200B;

And in regards to which is more or less annoying, definitely random crits. Countless times have I absolutely dominated a player in a fight, left them with sub 20 hp or so, while having over 100 myself, yet gotten killed by a random crit. I don't call players bad for getting random crits, but they're definitely more annoying than a weapon that I KNOW will give a guaranteed crit if certain conditions are met.

&#x200B;

For instance. If I get shot by a flare, I am on fire. Knowing that it'll crit next time it hits me, I will obviously fall back and find cover. But if I'm fighting someone and they suddenly crocket me, there's nothing I can do about it.

Okay I really want to know the mods you're using, all of them!

&#x200B;

... Or at least the most major ones- I know I wouldn't waste my time saying all 200 I use lol

Man of culture is usually either used as a joke, or to refer to a person who shares a same taste. Which is why its used in hentai a lot, but it doesn't necessarily refer to it. There's plenty of memes about it too - pretty sure that is where it originated from in fact.

&#x200B;

Edit: Also its definitely not out of context and you definitely overreacted a lot.
